From 74b16148789c91f7c1622c30b17c26efb383e59b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 10:30:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ci: the cpu-ubuntu job runs protected-win validate, so the
 manifest is gated where the code is

HANDOFF-FROM-R15B.md section 7 and the R17 prompt step 5 asked for a
`protected-win validate` step in CI; no job had one (R17B check F8). The
manifest (tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json) is a file class every base
move rewrites, and its symbols class (WI-1700) is the only gate that sees a
definition deleted while its declaration survives. One step on the CPU job,
python3 + git only, before the build, so a manifest that no longer matches
the tree fails the run before a compiler is even invoked.

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-210 R17C (Fable 5.1 MEDIUM, kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - CI workflow only; never run, the branch is not pushed
WI: WI-1702
Lane: lane-210
---
 .github/workflows/arifi-backends-matrix.yml | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/arifi-backends-matrix.yml b/.github/workflows/arifi-backends-matrix.yml
index 666b5edd0..8ac9f1556 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/arifi-backends-matrix.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/arifi-backends-matrix.yml
@@ -92,6 +92,15 @@ jobs:
       - name: Dependencies
         run: sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y ninja-build cmake libssl-dev
 
+      - name: protected-win validate (manifest vs tree)
+        shell: bash
+        run: |
+          # the protected-win manifest is code too: every registered mechanism must still
+          # be present in the tree (anchors) and DEFINED (symbols class, WI-1700). Runs on
+          # the CPU job because it needs only python3 and git; it gates the manifest file
+          # class where the code is, instead of only on the rig.
+          python3 tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py protected-win validate --ref HEAD
+
       - name: Configure + build
         run: |
           set -o pipefail
@@ -248,11 +257,25 @@ jobs:
           # bf0c4aecc rewrote ggml-metal-ops.cpp and ggml-metal-device.cpp; device.m is the
           # library loader (lane-210 part 2 found it referencing the per-kind split's
           # symbols without their declarations - this is the step that proves or refutes it)
-          for f in ggml-metal-ops.cpp.o ggml-metal-device.cpp.o ggml-metal-device.m.o ggml-metal-tuning.cpp.o; do
+          for f in ggml-metal-ops.cpp.o ggml-metal-device.cpp.o ggml-metal-device.m.o ggml-metal-tuning.cpp.o ggml-metal-moe-cache.mm.o; do
             hit=$(find build/ggml/src/ggml-metal -name "$f" | head -n1)
             if [ -z "$hit" ]; then echo "MISSING object for $f"; exit 1; fi
             echo "ok  $hit"
           done
+          # lane-210 part 3 (R17C): the ArifiLabs kernel set is its own library kind. embed=ON
+          # must have produced its embedded blob, embed=OFF its metallib, or every TQ/turbo
+          # kernel is unreachable at runtime while the build stays green.
+          if [ "${{ matrix.embed }}" = "ON" ]; then
+            hit=$(find build/ggml/src/ggml-metal -name "ggml-metal-embed-arifi.s" | head -n1)
+            if [ -z "$hit" ]; then echo "MISSING embedded arifi library"; exit 1; fi
+            echo "ok  $hit"
+          else
+            for f in default.metallib ggml-arifi.metallib; do
+              hit=$(find build/bin -name "$f" | head -n1)
+              if [ -z "$hit" ]; then echo "MISSING $f"; exit 1; fi
+              echo "ok  $hit"
+            done
+          fi
 
       - name: test-quantize-fns (CPU, baselined)
         shell: bash
